\n```\n344 | def _maybe_right_yaxis(self, ax: Axes, axes_num):\n345 |         if not self.on_right(axes_num):\n346 |             # secondary axes may be passed via ax kw\n347 |             return self._get_ax_layer(ax)\n348 | \n349 |         if hasattr(ax, \"right_ax\"):\n350 |             # if it has right_ax property, ``ax`` must be left axes\n351 |             return ax.right_ax\n352 |         elif hasattr(ax, \"left_ax\"):\n353 |             # if it has left_ax property, ``ax`` must be right axes\n354 |             return ax\n355 |         else:\n356 |             # otherwise, create twin axes\n357 |             orig_ax, new_ax = ax, ax.twinx()\n358 |             # TODO: use Matplotlib public API when available\n359 |             new_ax._get_lines = orig_ax._get_lines\n360 |             new_ax._get_patches_for_fill = orig_ax._get_patches_for_fill\n361 |             orig_ax.right_ax, new_ax.left_ax = new_ax, orig_ax\n362 | \n363 |             if not self._has_plotted_object(orig_ax):  # no data on left y\n364 |                 orig_ax.get_yaxis().set_visible(False)\n365 | \n366 |             if self.logy is True or self.loglog is True:\n367 |                 new_ax.set_yscale(\"log\")\n368 |             elif self.logy == \"sym\" or self.loglog == \"sym\":\n369 |                 new_ax.set_yscale(\"symlog\")\n370 |             return new_ax\n```\n"}, {"content": "It appears that the search for `_setup_subplots` did not yield the expected function content due to a misalignment in line numbers. Let's try to retrieve the entire `_setup_subplots` function by searching for its exact definition.\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=file_path_or_pattern>pandas/plotting/_matplotlib/core.py</parameter>\n<parameter=search_terms>[\"_setup_subplots\"]\n</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"_setup_su